course: dictionary
lesson: 3172
title: Words about work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An employee is a person who works for a company, or for another person, and is paid for the work. Clues in the sentence tell you this: the word «employees» sits next to words about jobs and pay.
explain: The example «"Independent contractor" means a worker without the rights and benefits of an employee, such as sick pay, holiday pay and a safe job (US).» uses the word without to show a difference. An independent contractor is a worker who does not get the same rights as an employee.
explain: The third example shows a crime. «It was reported that scammers used a deepfake video call, pretending to be a company boss, to get an employee to send a huge amount of money.» The scammers fooled the employee by pretending to be the boss, so employees can be targets too.
fact: An employee is a person who works for a company or another person and is paid for it.
fact: Employees are often paid wages, usually per hour or per week.
fact: A full-time employee works the main hours of the working week; a part-time employee works fewer hours.
fact: «Employee of the month» is a title given to a worker who is chosen for praise at work.
fact: «Associate» often means an ordinary, low-paid employee, especially in US shops.
exercise: Ali says, «An employee is the boss of the company.» What is an employee really? | *A person who works for a company or another person and is paid | A bank that lends money | The owner who never does any work | A person who buys things in a shop
exercise: «It was reported that scammers used a deepfake video call, pretending to be a company boss, to get an employee to send a huge amount of money.» Who was tricked? | The scammers | The bank | *An employee | The company boss
exercise: «"Independent contractor" means a worker without the rights and benefits of an employee, such as sick pay.» What does independent contractor mean? | *A worker without the rights and benefits of an employee | A boss who owns the company | An employee who gets extra sick pay | A machine that pays wages
test: What is a part-time employee? | *Someone who works fewer hours than a full-time employee | Someone who does not get paid | Someone who works all day and every day | A boss who owns a shop
test: In US shops, what does «associate» often mean? | The owner of the shop | *An ordinary, low-paid employee | A scammer pretending to be a boss | A customer who pays with cash
exam: Which statement about an employee is true? | An employee is always the boss | *An employee works for a company or another person and is paid for it | An employee never gets paid | An employee owns the company they work for
